  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Man Smart Woman Smarter**: back after 92 archived shows (1219 days); rare: 10 archived performances [8]\n- **Queen Jane Approximately**: back after 88 archived shows (1213 days); rare: 4 archived performances [8]\n- **Deep Elem Blues**: back after 49 archived shows (835 days); rare: 6 archived performances [8]\n- **Liberty**: rare: 13 archived performances [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2021-10-14.DosEquisPavilionDallasTX** (recommended): audience recording; 18 songs; 191 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [1]\n- **deadco2021-10-14.AKG_mix**: source not stated; 18 songs; 185 min; rated 2.5/5 by 2 [3]. Said about its sound: Volume at the venue was very low, possibly due to state fair regulations, and vocals sat relatively low in the mix [3]\n- **deadco2021-10-14.Schoeps**: source not stated; 18 songs; 182 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The reviewer reads the night's setlist as a quiet rebuttal aimed at the Texas government, with strong playing behind it [6]\n- Lineup listed: Bob Weir on guitar and vocals, John Mayer on guitar and vocals, Oteil Burbridge on bass and vocals [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2021-10-14.DosEquisPavilionDallasTX**: taped by W. Zimmerman; transferred by JT/NY; source: Aud > Sennheiser Me-80 Mini Shotguns> GakCables > Mix Pre 6 @ 16/48 [1]. Also: Audience recording using Sennheiser ME-80 mini shotgun mics into a Mix Pre 6 at 16/48, edited in Sound Forge Pro 13, converted to FLAC [1]\n- **deadco2021-10-14.AKG_mix**: taped by CorFit Chris; transferred by InsideOut Recording; source: AKG ck61 + ck63 > SD MixPre-6 [3]. Also: Two mic sources, AKG 461 and AKG ck63, into a MixPre-6, placed seven feet high at the back of the sound cage; processed by Chris at InsideOut Recording [3]\n- **deadco2021-10-14.Schoeps**: taped by Hellion; transferred by Chris Hale; source: Schoeps MK22 > Tascam DR680 [2]",
